1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,360
You are one of
the Seafolk, correct?

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,490
What if I am?

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,990
You must be another soldier...

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:13,830
I am here to eliminate you.

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:34,100
Was that...

6
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,850
the last of them?

7
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,350
Wow!

8
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,770
- Awesome!
- Amazing!

9
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,150
They must have been desperate.

10
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:51,910
Now I'm angry.

11
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:54,990
I will tear you to shreds.

12
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,910
I let my guard down again.

13
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,910
I never learn.

14
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,130
Saitama...

15
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,090
You're Class C, rank 2.

16
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:06,880
Are you sure?

17
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:07,840
Yeah.

18
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,260
Hurry it up. It's raining.

19
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:14,560
He burst through every record
during the fitness exam...

20
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:17,770
And he worked with some Class S
heroes to destroy that meteor.

21
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:22,940
But because he came out of nowhere,
people are saying he's a fraud.

22
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:26,070
Any other class C hero I'd stop...

23
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:33,740
This may be our chance to see
how strong he truly is.

24
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:39,620
Saitama, here's the location.
Head there immediately.

25
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:52,970
UNYIELDING JUSTICE

26
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,060
One punch

27
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:11,520
Three, two, one, kill shot

28
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:15,280
He joins the fight, he wins, the strongest in history

29
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,280
Are you talking to him? Frustration ☹

30
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,780
He's not going to stop

31
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:22,910
One punch, that's it, one fight after another

32
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:26,540
He wins, he always wins, overwhelmingly

33
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:30,370
Power, get power

34
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,340
On to the very edge

35
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,550
Hero

36
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:37,710
There are voices praising him

37
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:40,760
but he's not doing this for acclaim

38
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,010
Hero

39
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:46,770
So he just fight evil without end

40
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,230
Nobody knows who he is

41
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:52,400
Enemies to fight are numerous as the stars

42
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,480
and he's not gonna turn his back on you

43
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:56,820
Hero

44
00:02:56,820 --> 00:03:01,820
He's made up his mind and ain't gonna yield

45
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:09,040
A fighting hero

46
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,210
A lone hero

47
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:11,880
I

48
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:12,540
I

49
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:13,170
I

50
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:14,130
I

51
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:14,800
I

52
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,340
I

53
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:20,590
I wanna be the strongest hero

54
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:28,270
Those who can walk,
leave the shelter now!

55
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,690
I cannot promise I will win.

56
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,690
Run, while I keep him busy!

57
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:43,960
None of you monkeys
will escape me!

58
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:10,980
Lightning Eye!

59
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:15,240
I can't see...

60
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,450
Machinegun Blows!

61
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:28,830
You do like combo attacks,
don't you?

62
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:40,800
You can do it!

63
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,930
Quiet!

64
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,140
Now you melt, girl.

65
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,760
If you'd focused on me,

66
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:26,720
you could have easily dodged
my little ball of acid.

67
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:30,520
Instead, you chose to
sacrifice yourself to save a runt.

68
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:35,400
You're a fool, but I give you credit
for giving me a few scratches.

69
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,940
Of course, they've already healed.

70
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:40,410
Now, die.

71
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:43,570
Justice Crash!!

72
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:54,670
The Cyclist for Justice,
Mumen Rider is here!

73
00:05:56,730 --> 00:05:58,840
The top hero in Class C?

74
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:00,930
D-Don't...

75
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,680
It's Mumen Rider!

76
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:05,430
Mumen Rider came for us.

77
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:07,470
But he...

78
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,390
I'm bored already.

79
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:31,750
Oh, my apologies.
I nearly forgot to kill you.

80
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:35,840
Justice Tackle...

81
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:46,430
No one expects much—

82
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,940
...from me.

83
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:57,980
They think a Class C hero
won't be much help.

84
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:05,950
I know that better than anyone!

85
00:07:06,130 --> 00:07:08,620
I'm not good enough for Class B.

86
00:07:09,430 --> 00:07:13,040
I'm weak. I know that much.

87
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,500
No one has to tell me I have
no chance of beating you.

88
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:21,960
I already... know that!

89
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:27,300
What are you babbling about?
Begging for your life?

90
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,390
And yet, I must try.

91
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,480
It's not about winning or losing!

92
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:39,900
It's about me taking you on
right here, right now!

93
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:48,700
Enough of your rambling.
Time to finish you off.

94
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,870
You can do it!

95
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:56,790
Mumen Rider, you can do it!

96
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:01,880
You're the Cyclist for Justice!

97
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:06,880
Beat that weird monster, beat him!

98
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:09,390
You can do it!

99
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:11,930
Yeah, get him!

100
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,470
Beat him up!

101
00:08:13,470 --> 00:08:15,980
We're counting on you, Mumen Rider.

102
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,980
- You can do it!
- Beat him!

103
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,770
Good luck!

104
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:40,500
I think not!

105
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:48,380
You did fine. Nice fight.

106
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:54,260
Yet another piece of garbage
washed up on my shore?

107
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,980
H-Hey, Genos!

108
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,440
Are you still alive?!

109
00:09:01,210 --> 00:09:02,980
Mas...ter...

110
00:09:05,630 --> 00:09:07,360
Hang on for a second.

111
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:10,490
I've gotta pound this Seafreak
or whatever it's called.

112
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:13,660
I heard that!

113
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:23,750
Impressive. You're still on your feet
after one of my punches.

114
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:27,090
Clearly you're different
from the rest of this trash.

115
00:09:27,090 --> 00:09:30,720
Huh? Your punch was
too weak, that's all.

116
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:34,930
Hey, someone else is over there.
Who is that? A hero?

117
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,540
That head...

118
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:38,270
I remember it from
the Hero Registry.

119
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:40,770
I know him! He's a Class C rookie.

120
00:09:40,910 --> 00:09:42,770
I think he's Rank 2.

121
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:44,070
Class C?

122
00:09:44,070 --> 00:09:47,320
So we're still gonna get killed...

123
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:50,570
But that punch
didn't hurt him at all.

124
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,030
That's your imagination.

125
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,870
You saw how many heroes
were blown away

126
00:09:54,870 --> 00:09:56,540
by that thing's punches, right?

127
00:09:58,510 --> 00:10:02,750
I am the King of the Deep,
Lord of the Seas.

128
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:07,300
All life on Earth comes from the sea,
as if she were our mother.

129
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,970
In other words, as ruler of the seas,

130
00:10:09,970 --> 00:10:12,340
I am the pinnacle of a pyramid

131
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:15,890
that includes every living
organism on this world!

132
00:10:15,890 --> 00:10:17,660
To defy me, means

133
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:19,560
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

134
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:21,940
It's raining out, so let's do this.

135
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:47,500
Whaattt!!

136
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:48,960
Awesome!

137
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,300
That was amazing!

138
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:53,970
- Thank goodness!
- He did it!

139
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:06,810
Well... that was lame.
I kinda had my hopes up, too.

140
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:16,700
I'm back with my weapons.

141
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:20,950
But damn you, Deep Sea King.
You got away.

142
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,470
Hey, what's that?

143
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,510
It is the mail.

144
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:45,270
The post office cannot come here,
so the drone now delivers the mail.

145
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:47,110
The post office's drone?

146
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:50,020
No, it belongs to
the Hero Association.

147
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:51,820
I see.

148
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:58,820
The public sends these to the heroes,
much like fan letters.

149
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:01,950
Seriously? Are there any for me?

150
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:03,370
- There are.
-Oh! Let's go in and open them!

151
00:12:03,370 --> 00:12:04,670
TO C CLASS HERO SAITAMA

152
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:06,670
- Oh! Let's go in and open them!

153
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:12,800
I even joined your fan club!
I'm just crazy about you!

154
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:24,960
No one cares about you!
You Cowardly, Cheating Bastard

155
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:28,480
Damn it. I'll find out who sent it.

156
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:30,230
Here's a guy with free time.

157
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:39,820
All it took was one punch!

158
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:42,080
One punch! Just one!

159
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,950
Is he really Class C?

160
00:12:43,950 --> 00:12:44,950
He's too strong!

161
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:46,580
Or maybe...

162
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:50,580
...the monster wasn't really that tough?

163
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:54,010
Yeah, but so many heroes went down.

164
00:12:54,010 --> 00:12:57,720
That just means those
heroes were weaklings.

165
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:02,350
Maybe... I suppose the monster didn't
look all that tough when he killed it.

166
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:07,520
After all, a Class C hero
took it out with a single punch!

167
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:09,850
What's that say about
the heroes it beat?

168
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:13,110
They may call themselves
Class A or Class S,

169
00:13:13,110 --> 00:13:15,740
but their titles don't mean a thing.

170
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,530
Hey, enough of that.
They risked their lives for us.

171
00:13:20,710 --> 00:13:23,950
Risked their lives?
Anyone can do that.

172
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:26,370
But a "hero" has to beat monsters.

173
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:29,870
It all ended well this time,
so whatever.

174
00:13:29,870 --> 00:13:34,380
But it's annoying when heroes
who are really just average Joes

175
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,300
show up and try to save you.

176
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,920
If you're gonna call yourself
a hero, then—

177
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:40,020
Shut your fat mouth!

178
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:42,720
Why are you getting mad at me?

179
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,970
The Hero Association gets their funds
from our donations, right?

180
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:50,270
As long as we're paying for it,
they'd better protect us.

181
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:52,270
The fact of the matter is

182
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:55,190
that bald guy pretty much took
care of it all by himself.

183
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,070
So all the other heroes
died for nothing.

184
00:13:58,070 --> 00:14:01,400
Anyone can come up with a way
to buy a little time.

185
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:05,910
In the end, the other "heroes"
didn't do anything heroic.

186
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:06,870
I said shut up!

187
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:09,870
We were all saved.
Just leave it at that.

188
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:10,910
Exactly!

189
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:17,630
Today's my lucky day!

190
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:22,890
The other heroes wore the monster down,
so beating it was kid's play!

191
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:25,510
Good thing I was late.

192
00:14:25,570 --> 00:14:28,970
I barely did a thing and now
I get all the credit.

193
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:32,020
Hey, spread the word, all of you!

194
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,940
I'm the one who finished
the monster off!

195
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,900
I'll beat the snot out
of anyone who says

196
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:39,480
it's only 'cause I got here late!

197
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,030
What's he mean?

198
00:14:41,090 --> 00:14:42,780
The monster was already weak?

199
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:44,200
Huh...?

200
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,740
Hang on a sec. That's Saitama!

201
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,950
Saitama?

202
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:51,830
He's the hero from City Z
that everyone calls a cheat.

203
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,580
What? A cheat?

204
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:57,630
He appeared out of nowhere
and climbed the ranks super-fast.

205
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:58,800
Yeah, pretty fishy.

206
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,090
Hey, you guys!

207
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:03,470
Look after the fallen heroes, okay?

208
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:05,470
If they die on me,

209
00:15:05,470 --> 00:15:07,600
how am I gonna cash in
on their work?

210
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,930
He is a cheat!

211
00:15:08,930 --> 00:15:10,270
Man, that's no fair.

212
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:12,100
So he's just taking the credit?

213
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:15,900
Compared to him, the other heroes
seem a little more heroic.

214
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:19,150
Where would we be now...

215
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:20,940
if the other heroes hadn't fought?

216
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:24,780
Yeah, I feel so grateful to them all...

217
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:30,120
Master Saitama...

218
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,790
Is this really what you want?

219
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:35,040
Hey, it stopped raining.

220
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:41,340
If this is the path you choose to walk,
I will not interfere.

221
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:47,260
But in the future, if you are ever
forced into a corner by this,

222
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:50,270
at that moment, I will—

223
00:15:50,270 --> 00:15:52,270
Hey, there's one more.

224
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:58,360
Thanks!!

225
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,700
Someone's thanking me.

226
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:03,530
It must be someone you saved.

227
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,400
I see. Any left?

228
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:09,620
There is one from the Hero Association.

229
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,830
The Association?

230
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:12,790
Are they firing me?

231
00:16:12,970 --> 00:16:14,500
Well, whatever.

232
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:20,000
What's this? I'm Class C...rank 1?

233
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:22,050
CITY Z - HERO ASSOCIATION OFFICE

234
00:16:22,050 --> 00:16:24,970
So, why'd you call me in?

235
00:16:25,650 --> 00:16:28,220
When you registered with
the Hero Registry,

236
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:30,930
you were given
the Association handbook.

237
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:36,230
Haven't you read it?
It lists all our rules and regulations.

238
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,940
Yeah, I guess I've got it somewhere.

239
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:43,780
No matter. Congratulations on
attaining rank 1 in Class C.

240
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,780
Hm? Oh, I see.

241
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:48,780
So you guys are the ones
who decide the hero rankings.

242
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:52,530
There are more members
on the review board,

243
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:55,040
but the four of us here today
will be handling your interview.

244
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,710
Interview?

245
00:16:57,060 --> 00:17:02,500
The top ranking Class C hero is given
the option to be promoted to Class B.

246
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:06,210
However, if you wish to remain
in Class C, that's fine too.

247
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:08,220
How about it, Mr. Saitama?

248
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,010
Do you want to move up?

249
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:12,800
Although if you do, you'll be ranked
at the very bottom again.

250
00:17:13,110 --> 00:17:17,060
Either way's fine,
but I guess I'll try moving up.

251
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:20,360
There'll be no more
weekly quotas that way.

252
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:25,780
Besides, I can't stick to Class C
forever with Genos in Class S.

253
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,990
I see, so you want a promotion.

254
00:17:28,990 --> 00:17:31,200
First, we'll need you to
answer some questions

255
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,490
and undergo a psychiatric analysis.

256
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,580
This Saitama...

257
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:40,620
He's the one who finished off
the Deep Sea King.

258
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,920
What do you think?

259
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:44,130
Some say he's a fraud...

260
00:17:44,130 --> 00:17:47,300
He set new overall records
in the fitness exam,

261
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,420
so his physical ability is solid.

262
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:54,680
Well, according to rumors,
he cheated on the exams, too.

263
00:17:54,950 --> 00:17:56,720
Rumors are just rumors.

264
00:17:57,020 --> 00:18:00,190
No sense in doubting him now.

265
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,360
The bottom line is,
he wants to move up.

266
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:06,150
Why not let him go for now?

267
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:09,070
If he's for real,
he'll make it in Class B.

268
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:14,740
But if he's a fake, he'll soon regret it.

269
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:18,960
He is entering a cruel and callous world.

270
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,870
We'll cross that bridge when we must.

271
00:18:21,770 --> 00:18:23,790
Promotion to Class B?

272
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,750
You interrupted my filming for this?

273
00:18:27,750 --> 00:18:30,090
It's not something that
needs my attention.

274
00:18:30,090 --> 00:18:32,970
This is a decision for
the executive committee.

275
00:18:32,970 --> 00:18:34,090
Listen.

276
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:38,430
I only want input on managing
heroes Class A and above,

277
00:18:38,430 --> 00:18:41,020
since they have a strong impact on society.

278
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,770
As a hero in the same class,

279
00:18:42,770 --> 00:18:45,520
if they're inadequate,
it hurts my image too.

280
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,150
Especially this last incident...

281
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:51,030
It was beyond inadequate—
it was appalling.

282
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:53,280
Don't you agree?

283
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:57,990
Speaking of social impact,
the hero now wanting to move up

284
00:18:57,990 --> 00:19:01,790
is the one who finished off
the Deep Sea King.

285
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,810
UNKNOWN HEROES SNATCH VICTORY

286
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:24,940
Why the sour pusses?

287
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:27,860
That's no way to show off
those cute faces!

288
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,270
You?!

289
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:30,820
I thought you were in prison!

290
00:19:32,130 --> 00:19:34,490
I escaped just to see you!

291
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:37,780
Now... It's time for your Angel shots!

292
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:42,830
You guys! You need your meds!

293
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:49,960
A CLASS S FAILURE!!

294
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:58,970
So I'm Class B now...

295
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:01,850
Those tests took long enough.

296
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,680
Meh, not like I had to be somewhere.

297
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:07,480
Something smells good...

298
00:20:09,290 --> 00:20:10,480
Welcome.

299
00:20:12,490 --> 00:20:14,110
Assorted oden, please.

300
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:15,360
All right.

301
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,950
Want a drink?

302
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:20,950
If you're not drinking,
let me buy you a plate.

303
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:21,910
Why?

304
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,160
That.

305
00:20:24,250 --> 00:20:25,960
You were at the Association?

306
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:29,630
Let's celebrate your promotion.

307
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,880
Thanks

308
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,590
for giving me a ride.

309
00:20:40,150 --> 00:20:41,600
Should I walk?

310
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:44,560
N-No... I can handle it...

311
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:48,940
Hey, are you scared?

312
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:53,820
You got separated from
the Class S hero, Genos, right?

313
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,740
The enemy is threat level Demon.

314
00:20:56,990 --> 00:20:58,700
A monster so formidable that even if

315
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:01,870
the Class S and Class B heroes all
ganged up on him, they'd never win.

316
00:21:01,870 --> 00:21:03,620
So if you wanna run...

317
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,200
Are you Class S too?

318
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,830
No, I'm Class C.

319
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,750
Laugh if you want to.

320
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,090
I'm not laughing.

321
00:21:14,650 --> 00:21:19,430
It sure is tough making those
weekly quotas for us Class C's...

322
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,810
You're a funny guy.

323
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:29,520
I'm Mumen Rider.
A hero, just like you.

324
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:32,440
Huh?

325
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,030
Hey! Watch it!

326
00:21:35,630 --> 00:21:38,360
Oh! You're that guy!

327
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:40,780
I've been looking for you.

328
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:43,830
I couldn't say everything
in my letter.

329
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,870
Oh yeah.

330
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:53,210
Maybe some mozuku then?

331
00:21:53,210 --> 00:21:55,750
Hey! Give us your best mozuku!

332
00:21:55,810 --> 00:21:57,050
Comin' right up.

